  "description": "An ICME digital twin for material-failure prediction chains models across scales. CALPHAD phase equilibria fix the phase fractions produced by the heat-treatment route; a synthetic representative volume element (RVE) carries that microstructure into a DAMASK crystal-plasticity solve for local stress and strain; those fields are homogenised into an anisotropic material card for a component-level Abaqus analysis, and a Tanaka–Mura law converts the resolved shear history at hotspots into a crack-initiation life. Non-destructive inspection findings are fused in so the estimate reflects the actual part rather than the nominal one.\n\nThe output is a per-hotspot life distribution that gates the maintenance interval and feeds a fleet-wide materials data lake for re-calibration. Budget roughly EUR 60-120k for the first component family (solver seats, an RVE calibration campaign and one coupon test series); expect 4-6 months to a chain validated against existing coupon and full-scale fatigue data.\n\nIllustrative output — a saved generation shown for display only, not a delivered project.",
